<statement>
<p>Evaluate each of these by multiplying enough times.</p>
<p>
  <m>\displaystyle{2}^{{5}}=</m> <fillin characters="6"/></p>
<p>
  <m>\displaystyle{7}^{{3}}=</m> <fillin characters="6"/></p>
<p>
  <m>\displaystyle{1.3}^{{4}}=</m> <fillin characters="6"/></p>


</statement>
<answer>
<p><ul><li>32</li><li>343</li><li>2.8561</li></ul></p>
</answer>
<solution><p><m>\displaystyle{2}^{{5}}={2}\cdot{2}\cdot{2}\cdot{2}\cdot{2}={32}</m>.</p>
<p><m>\displaystyle{7}^{{3}}={7}\cdot{7}\cdot{7}={343}</m>.</p>
<p><m>\displaystyle{1.3}^{{5}}={1.3}\cdot{1.3}\cdot{1.3}\cdot{1.3}={2.8561}</m>.</p>
</solution>
</myopenmath>